1. DEFINITIONS

“Agreement Steward” means the Airbus Open Software Program Office (OSPO). The contact details can be
    found in the InnerSource License Charter.

“Airbus InnerSource Governance” means the software governance team. The contact details can be found
    in the InnerSource License Charter.

“As a Service” means that a Recipient provides the functionalities of a Program to a Customer or an
    Airbus Group company, by allowing them to interact with the Program remotely through a computer
    network.

“Inner Source License Charter” means the charter joined to this Agreement providing a
    non-comprehensive list of conditions to be checked by Contributors.

“Contribution” means:

    a) in the case of the Initial Contributor, the initial version of the software which is subject to
       this Agreement, and

    b) in the case of each Subsequent Contributor:

        i) changes to a Program, and
        ii) additions to a Program;

        where such changes and/or additions to the considered Program originate from and are Distributed by
        that Subsequent Contributor.

    A Contribution “originates” from a Contributor if it was added to the Program by such Contributor
    itself or anyone acting on such Contributor’s behalf. Contributions do not include additions to the
    Program which: (i) are separate modules of software Distributed in conjunction with the considered
    Program under their own license agreement, and (ii) are not Derivative Works of the considered
    Program.

“Contribute” means making a Contribution available in any manner that enables the transfer of a
    copy.

“Contributor” means an Airbus Group Company that Contributes.

   - The “Initial Contributor” is the originator of the initial version of the software which is
     subject to this Agreement.

   - The “Subsequent Contributor” is any other Contributor.

“Customer” means the end user of a Contribution or a Program that is not an Airbus Group Company.

“Derivative Works” shall mean any work, whether in Source Code or other form, that is based on (or
    derived from) a Program and constitutes an original work of authorship according to applicable law.

“Distribute” or “Distribution” means the acts of transmitting a Contribution or a Program to another
    Airbus Group Company or to a Customer.

“Airbus Group Company” means Airbus and any company or other legal entity with respect to which
    Airbus directly or indirectly holds over fifty percent (50%) of the nominal value of the issued
    share capital or over fifty percent (50%) of the voting power at the general meeting of shareholders
    or has the power to appoint a majority of the directors or otherwise directs the activities of such
    company or other legal entity.

“Executable Code” means the compilation of a Source Code module into machine code.

“Larger Work” means a work that combines a Program with a software or a library licensed under
    another license than this Agreement. “Program” means either the

   (i) initial version of a software which is subject to this Agreement, or
   (ii) the combination of Contributions in accordance with this Agreement.

“Recipient” means any legal entity who is authorized to reproduce and to Distribute a Contribution
    or a Program under this Agreement as long as said entity is and remains an Airbus Group Company.

“Source Code” means the computer program in a programming language that can be understood by human
    beings, including documentation and configuration files thereof.

2. GRANT OF RIGHTS

a) Subject to the terms of this Agreement, each Contributor hereby grants Recipient:

   (i) a non-exclusive, worldwide right to reproduce, display, perform, and where the Source Code of
       the Contribution has been made available by said Contributor and subject to Article 3.1 to modify,
       complete and/or prepare Derivative Works of the concerned Contribution, as long as Recipient remains
       an Airbus Group Company; and

   (ii) a non-exclusive, worldwide right to Distribute to an Airbus Group Company only, the
       Contribution of such Contributor, in Source Code, Executable Code form or As a Service, as long as
       Recipient remains an Airbus Group Company; and

   (iii) a non-exclusive, worldwide right to Distribute the Contribution of such Contributor to a
       Customer, in Executable Code form or As a Service only and as part of a Larger Work, as long as
       Recipient remains an Airbus Group Company.

b) Recipient understands that although each Contributor grants the rights set forth herein, no
   assurances are provided by any Contributor that a Contribution or a Program does not infringe the
   patent or other intellectual property rights of any other entity. Each Contributor disclaims any
   liability to Recipient for claims brought by any other Airbus Group Company or any third party based
   on infringement of intellectual property rights or otherwise.

   As a condition to exercising the rights granted hereunder, each Recipient hereby assumes sole
   responsibility to secure any other intellectual property rights needed, if any. For example, if a
   third party patent license is required to allow Recipient to Distribute a Contribution or a Program,
   it is Recipient’s responsibility to acquire that license before distributing said Contribution or
   Program.

c) Each Contributor represents that to its knowledge it has sufficient rights in its Contribution,
   to grant the rights set forth in this Agreement.

d) Each Contributor undertakes to comply with the InnerSource License Charter.

e) Except as expressly stated here above, Recipient receives no rights or licenses to the
   intellectual property of any Contributor under this Agreement, whether expressly, by implication or
   otherwise. All rights in the Program not expressly granted under this Agreement are reserved.

3. REQUIREMENTS

The grant of rights according to section 2 is subject to the following requirements:

3.1 APPROVAL OF MODIFICATIONS BY INITIAL CONTRIBUTOR

In case the Recipient modifies, completes and/or prepares Derivative Works of the Program, the
Recipient shall provide the Source Code of such modification, completion and/or Derivative Works of
the Program to the Initial Contributor for approval prior to any Distribution. In case that the
Initial Contributor – at its sole discretion – does not approve such modification, completion and/or
Derivative Work the Program containing such modification, completion and/or Derivative Work shall
not be Distributed.

3.2 MODIFICATIONS BY THIRD PARTIES

Recipient may authorize third parties to modify, complete and/or prepare Derivative Works of the
Program on its behalf only if (i) there are compelling technical or regulatory reasons to do so, or
(ii) the Initial Contributor is not willing or not able to make such modifications, completions
and/or Derivative Works on request of the Recipient on commercial terms to be agreed.

3.3 DISTRIBUTION TO A LEGAL ENTITY WHICH IS NOT AN AIRBUS GROUP COMPANY

A Recipient may Distribute a Program to a legal entity which is not an Airbus Group Company in
Executable Code form or As a Service and only as part of and included in its Larger Work or software
solution under its own license agreement, provided that:

    a) it agrees to bear all warranties and liabilities related to the use of the Program; and

    b) the rights granted to the Customer are limited to the right to reproduce, display and perform
       said Contribution or Program.

3.4 DISTRIBUTION TO AN AIRBUS GROUP COMPANY

A Recipient may Distribute a Program in Source Code form to an Airbus Group Company provided that a
copy of this Agreement is included with each copy of the Program.

If the Recipient Distributes the Program (whether with or without its own Contributions) to an
Airbus Group Company it must be licensed under the terms of this Agreement. The Recipient that
Distributes the Program cannot offer or impose any additional terms or conditions on the Program
that alter or restrict the terms of this Agreement.

A Recipient may not remove or alter any copyright and/or ownership notices contained within a
Contribution or a Program. Each Contributor must identify itself as the originator of its
Contribution, in a manner that reasonably allows subsequent Recipients to identify the originator of
the Contribution.

3.5 GENERAL LIMITATIONS OF USE

Recipient is not permitted to Distribute the Program as a stand-alone product or to Distribute a
Program containing modification, completion and/or Derivative Work not approved by the Initial
Contributor.

3.6 SHARING OF TEST RESULTS

The Recipient shall submit to the Initial Contributor any available test results (including any
detected faults) regarding the implementation or integration of a Contribution or Program.

3.7 CONTRIBUTION TO THE MAINTENANCE OF THE PROGRAM

When the Recipient receives the Program, and subsequently at each anniversary date of that date as
long as the Recipient uses the Program, it shall pay to the Initial Contributor a fee that is
equivalent to a reasonable share of the annual maintenance costs of the Program incurred by the
Initial Contributor. Under no circumstances shall the fee exceed 50% of the Initial Contributor´s
actual annual maintenance cost.

Through this mechanism the Recipient will benefit from any maintenance work performed by the Initial
Contributor including any updates of the Program that the Initial Contributor may Distribute from
time to time.

4. LIABILITY IN CASE OF COMMERCIAL DISTRIBUTION

Commercial distributors of software may accept certain responsibilities with respect to customers,
end users, business partners and the like. While this license is intended to facilitate the
commercial use of a Contribution or a Program, the Recipient who includes a Contribution or a
Program in a commercial product offering should do so in a manner which does not create potential
liability for other Contributors. Therefore, if a Recipient includes a Contribution or a Program in
a commercial product offering, such Recipient (“Commercial Distributor”) hereby agrees to defend and
indemnify every other Contributor (“Indemnified Contributor”) against any losses, damages and costs
(collectively “Losses”) arising from claims, lawsuits and other legal actions brought by a third
party against the Indemnified Contributor to the extent caused by the acts or omissions of such
Commercial Distributor in connection with its Distribution of the Contribution Program in a
commercial product offering.

The obligations in this section do not apply to any claims or Losses relating to any actual or
alleged intellectual property infringement.

In order to qualify, an Indemnified Contributor must:

    a) promptly notify the Commercial Distributor in writing of such claim, and

    b) allow the Commercial Distributor to control, and cooperate with the Commercial Distributor in,
       the defense and any related settlement negotiations.

The Indemnified Contributor may participate in any such claim at its own expense.

For example, a Recipient might include a Program in a commercial product offering, product X. That
Recipient is then a Commercial Distributor. If that Commercial Distributor then makes performance
claims, or offers warranties related to product X, those performance claims and warranties are such
Commercial Distributor’s responsibility alone. Under this section, the Commercial Distributor would
have to defend claims against the other Contributors related to those performance claims and
warranties, and if a court requires any other Contributor to pay any damages as a result, the
Commercial Distributor must pay those damages.

