Contribution or Program or the exercise of any rights granted hereunder, even if advised of the
possibility of such damages.

7. GENERAL

7.1. VALIDITY OF THIS AGREEMENT

If any provision of this Agreement is invalid or unenforceable under applicable law, it shall not
affect the validity or enforceability of the remainder of the terms of this Agreement and such
provision shall be interpreted and reformed to the minimum extent necessary to make such provision
valid and enforceable.

7.2. NEW VERSIONS OF THIS AGREEMENT

Everyone is permitted to copy and distribute copies of this Agreement, but in order to avoid
inconsistency, this Agreement may only be modified in the following manner:

The Agreement Steward reserves the right to publish new versions (including revisions) of this
Agreement from time to time. No one other than the Agreement Steward has the right to modify this
Agreement. The Agreement Steward may assign the responsibility to serve as Agreement Steward to
another company, whether an Airbus Group Company or not. Each new version of this Agreement will be
given a distinguishing version number.

A Contribution or a Program is always Contributed according to the ongoing version of the Agreement.
Furthermore, a Contributor may elect to have any following version of the Agreement apply to one or
several of its Contribution(s).

8. LICENSE TERMINATION

All Recipient’s rights under this Agreement shall terminate if Recipient fails to comply with any of
the material terms or conditions of this Agreement and does not cure such failure in a reasonable
period of time after becoming aware of such noncompliance and/or if the Recipient ceases to be an
Airbus Group Company.

In case of termination of this Agreement, Recipient agrees to cease use and Distribution of the
Program as soon as reasonably practicable.

In case Recipient has become a Contributor the license granted by the Recipient (having become a
Contributor) under the terms of this Agreement with respect to its Contribution shall not be
affected in case the Recipient ceases to be an Airbus Group Company.

9. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

This Agreement shall be construed and governed according to the substantive laws of France, without
reference to rules of conflicts or choice of law.

Any dispute, controversy or claim arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be
settled by the Airbus InnerSource Governance.

If a dispute, controversy or claim can’t be settled by this governance, it shall be settled by the
Senior Management of the relevant business unit(s).

The mediation should not exceed a two (2) months period starting from the nomination of the
mediator. In case no settlement is reached by mediation, the dispute shall be referred to and
finally determined by arbitration in accordance with the WIPO Expedited Arbitration Rules. The
arbitral tribunal shall consist of a sole arbitrator. The place of arbitration shall be Paris. The
language to be used in the arbitral proceedings shall be English.

